You could use pgfplotstable and the xcolor
package with the [table]
option, which gives you the \cellcolor
command.

Here's a new style for \pgfplotstabletypeset
that colors the cell a different shade of gray according to the cell value, and prints the value in white if the background is more than 50% black.

The command

\pgfplotstabletypeset[color cells]{
x,a,b,c,d % The first column needs a name
a,90,10,0,0
b,0,80,10,10
c,0,0,95,5
d,0,10,5,85
}

